course: dictionary
lesson: 10068
title: The letters th
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Th is not one letter. It is two letters, t and h, that work together to make one sound, so it is called a digraph. Say «think» and notice that your tongue touches your teeth for the sound.
explain: In English, th has two sounds. The soft th is in «think» and «bath», where your voice does not buzz. The buzzy th is in «this» and «that», where your voice does buzz. Put your fingers on your throat and feel the difference.
explain: The ending -th is a different job. It turns a number into an order, like 4th, 5th and 20th, and it makes fractions like a fifth or a tenth. Th on its own can also be a short form, as in Th for Thursday.
fact: Th is a digraph: two letters making one sound, like sh, ch and ng.
fact: Soft th sounds like «think»; buzzy th sounds like «this».
fact: The ending -th makes ordinal numbers, such as 4th, 5th and 20th, and fractions, such as a fifth and a tenth.
fact: «Th» can also be an abbreviation for Thursday.
fact: In French, th has no th sound: it is just a t, so «le thé» (tea) is "luh TAY".
exercise: Which word has a buzzy th sound, as in «this»? | *this | think | thumb
exercise: What does the -th in «5th» show? | A question about a fraction | *Its place in order, the fifth one | A letter that makes no sound
exercise: What does «Th» mean on a calendar? | Thirteen | The | *Thursday
test: Which phrase means one of five equal parts? | thirty | fifth place | *one fifth
test: How many letters make the th sound in «think»? | Three | *Two | One
exam: In French, «le thé» (tea) is "luh TAY", so the th in thé makes just the sound of which letter? | th | *t | s | h
